//! Tokens produced by a real issuer, frozen.
//!
//! Verification has to be tested, and the code that mints tokens is not in this
//! repository. Rather than keep a minter here so the tests have something to
//! check, the tests check these: tokens generated once by the issuer and
//! written down.
//!
//! This is how cryptographic code should be tested anyway. A round trip against
//! your own minter passes even when both halves share a misunderstanding of the
//! format; a frozen vector fails the moment the format moves, which is the
//! failure worth catching. If these stop verifying, the wire format changed and
//! every token already in someone's hands has stopped working.
//!
//! Regenerating them requires the issuer, and is therefore a deliberate act.

